    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm looking at some paperwork for a house i'm trying to buy in seattle and it keeps mentioning \"escrow.\" i'm super confused lol. what does an escrow agent actually do and why do they need to hold my money for a while? thanks!",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Don't worry, escrow can seem confusing at first! An escrow agent is a neutral third party that holds the funds for both you and the seller until specific conditions are met in a real estate transaction, such as the inspection and financing falling into place. They distribute the funds only when these conditions are fulfilled, ensuring a smooth transfer of ownership and preventing disputes. Think of them as a safeguard to ensure both parties receive their share of the purchase price.",
